  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A circle passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and touches the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Which one of the following equations can represent a diameter of this circle ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>axis</mi></math> is tangent to the circle therefore the centre of the circle would be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and distance of centre from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;should be equal.<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, centre&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is&nbsp;the diameter, as centre lies on it.</p>"
  }
}